      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start on the content, but I just ran it through the tool and the thoroughness score is actually quite low compared to some of the other draft assistants. It's flagging it as \"low structural complexity.\" \n\nI don't want you to do anything stupid or just add \"Introduction\" and \"Summary\" headers, but maybe there's a way to be more granular with the critique? Like, instead of one big \"Methodology Critique\" block, could you break it down into more specific technical areas? It needs to feel more \"comprehensive\" for the system to rank it highly, but I still need it to actually be a useful, professional review. \n\nCan you try a version that has more detailed organizational structure to improve that score?",
